<subpara id="RM0000026WT004X_01" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___0000D2Y00000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>A three-way catalytic converter is used to efficiently purify the CO, HC and NOx in the exhaust gas. This three-way catalytic converter functions most efficiently near the stoichiometric air-fuel ratio. For this reason, CO, HC and NOx cannot be efficiently purified unless the engine is accurately controlled near the stoichiometric air-fuel ratio. The oxygen sensor is installed for the purpose of this control. The oxygen sensor has the characteristic of outputting a voltage proportional to the air-fuel ratio, and the engine control computer controls the air-fuel ratio based on that voltage. The heated oxygen sensor has a heater that warms the zirconia element. The heater is controlled by the engine control computer, and current flows to the heater to prevent the oxygen sensor from cooling and becoming unable to operate accurately when the exhaust gas temperature is low (such as when the intake air volume is small).</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A115539J02" width="7.106578999in" height="3.779676365in"/>
</figure>
